        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64894,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64895,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vagina</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64896,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These have occurred in patients aged 38&ndash;51&nbsp;years and usually present with symptoms related to a vaginal mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64897,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are extremely rare neoplasms, with only a single series of 4&nbsp;cases reported {31857682}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64898,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64899,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The reported cases were associated with high-risk HPV (types 16, 18, and 31). Some have arisen from vaginal adenosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64900,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These typically present as a polypoid mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64901,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histologically, these neoplasms are characterized by papillary, villoglandular, and/or glandular architecture. They exhibit morphological features characteristic of high-risk HPV&ndash;associated cervical adenocarcinomas, with columnar cells showing mucinous or mucin-poor (so-called pseudoendometrioid) features and crowded, cigar-shaped to ovoid irregular nuclei. Mitoses (mostly apical) and apoptotic bodies are typically easily identified. The tumours exhibit diffuse immunoreactivity with p16, characteristic of a high-risk HPV&ndash;associated neoplasm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64902,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/305\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Adenocarcinoma, HPV-associated, of the uterine cervix</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T13:50:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64903,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64904,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> apical mitoses and apoptotic bodies easily identifiable at low power; enlarged, hyperchromatic pseudostratified nuclei; exophytic papillary growth (villoglandular); absence of endometrioid-confirmatory features (squamous metaplasia, endometriosis); a cervical primary must be excluded; p16 overexpression.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> HPV detection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64905,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other vaginal neoplasms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64906,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Data are limited, but in the only published series, one tumour exhibited local recurrence after surgery {31857682}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:07:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]